      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "98b61dc9-d357-5388-aa7c-48c30e91d4a5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vaidotas, Wojdat, Kęstutis, Algirdas, Jogaila\n- Roles: Grand Duke of Lithuania, Duke of Trakai, ruler of medieval Lithuania\n- Places: Lithuania, Kreva\n\nFacts:\n- Kęstutis was born around 1297.\n- From 1342 to 1382, Kęstutis governed the Grand Duchy of Lithuania together with his brother Algirdas until 1377 and with his nephew Jogaila until 1381.\n- In 1362, Vaidotas, also called Wojdat, was a son of Kęstutis, Grand Duke of Lithuania.\n- Kęstutis was a ruler of medieval Lithuania and held the title Duke of Trakai.\n- Kęstutis died on 3 August or 15 August 1382 in Kreva.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5b45c0ca-f473-56e5-a374-3ca6f175e0cc",
        "text": "Page: Vaidotas. Sentence: Vaidotas or Wojdat (fl.\nPage: Vaidotas. Sentence: 1362) was a son of Kęstutis, Grand Duke of Lithuania.\nPage: Kęstutis. Sentence: Kęstutis (] ; born ca. 1297, died on 3 August or 15 August 1382 in Kreva) was a ruler of medieval Lithuania.\nPage: Kęstutis. Sentence: He was the Duke of Trakai and governed the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, 1342–82, together with his brother Algirdas (until 1377), and with his nephew Jogaila (until 1381).",
